# Risk engine

Pure functions, no I/O. Every rule below has a boundary test.

## Levels

`IntEnum`: `LOW=0, MODERATE=1, HIGH=2, SEVERE=3, NO_TRAVEL=4`. `UNKNOWN` when data is missing (excluded from avg, shown in UI, never coerced to LOW).

## Thresholds (lower bound inclusive)

| Level | Wind mph | Rain in/hr | Snow in/hr |
|---|---|---|---|
| LOW | < 25 | < 0.10 | < 0.5 |
| MODERATE | 25–34 | 0.10–<0.25 | 0.5–<1.0 |
| HIGH | 35–44 | 0.25–<0.50 | 1.0–<2.0 |
| SEVERE | 45–54 | 0.50–1.00 | 2.0–3.0 |
| NO_TRAVEL | ≥ 55 | > 1.00 | > 3.0 |

Wind input = `max(sustained, gust)`. Checkpoint level = `max(wind_level, rain_level, snow_level)`.

## Load rules (wind only, applied before the max)

- wind ≥ 55 → NO_TRAVEL (any load)
- 45–54 and load > 30,000 lb → NO_TRAVEL
- 35–44 and load > 40,000 lb → SEVERE

Express thresholds as data (tuples of upper bounds), not if-chains:

```python
# ❌ if rain < 0.10: ... elif rain < 0.25: ... (×3 copies)
# ✅ one `level_for(value, bands)` + a band table per condition
```

## Mile attribution & ranking

- Each checkpoint owns half the distance to each neighbor; owned miles sum to route length (assert in tests).
- `avg_risk` = distance-weighted mean of known levels.
- Rank key ascending: `(no_travel_mi, severe_mi, high_mi, avg_risk, duration_s)`. Recommend rank-1 always; attach warnings if NO_TRAVEL miles or incomplete weather on winner. Return tie-break reason for UI.

## Required tests

Every band edge (24.9/25/34.9/35/…/54.9/55; 0.0999/0.10/0.25/0.50/1.00/1.0001; snow equivalents), both load rules at 30,000 / 30,001 / 40,000 / 40,001 lb, gust > sustained, mile sum invariant, each ranking tie-break.
